module j3.data.save
    `key=int`, `key f=`, `key s=`, and `key b=` (hex) text. No serde.
    Any thread: no module state, so a worker can use a value it owns (`j3c doc threads`).

struct Save
    In-memory `key=int` save blob backed by an arena.
    bytes: []u8
        Raw file text (`key=value` lines).
    arena: &Arena
        Arena used when rewriting entries.

fn empty(arena: &Arena): Save
    Empty save with no entries.
fn load(path: string, arena: &Arena): Save
    Load a save file, or an empty save if the read fails.
fn getInt(s: &Save, key: string, fallback: int): int
    Parse the integer for `key`, or `fallback` if missing or malformed.
fn parseInt(bytes: []u8, i: int, fallback: int): int
    Parse an integer at `i`, or `fallback` when no digits are there.
fn putInt(s: &Save, key: string, v: int)
    Set or replace `key=v`, dropping any prior line for that key.
fn getFloat(s: &Save, key: string, fallback: f32): f32
    Parse the float for `key` (`key f=`), or `fallback` if missing.
fn putFloat(s: &Save, key: string, v: f32)
    Set or replace `key f=v`.
fn getStr(s: &Save, key: string, fallback: string): string
    The string for `key` (`key s=`), or `fallback` if missing.
fn putStr(s: &Save, key: string, v: string)
    Set or replace `key s=v`. Newlines in `v` are stored as spaces.
fn getBlob(s: &Save, key: string): []u8
    Decode the hex blob for `key` (`key b=`). Empty when missing.
fn putBlob(s: &Save, key: string, data: []u8)
    Set or replace `key b=` with the hex of `data`.
fn parseFloat(bytes: []u8, i: int): f32
    Parse a float at `i`. Stops at the first non-number byte.
fn store(s: &Save, path: string)
    Write the save bytes to `path`; write errors are ignored.
fn userDir(game: string): string
    Per-user folder for a game's saves, made if missing: Linux `$XDG_DATA_HOME/<game>` else `~/.local/share/<game>`,
    Windows `%APPDATA%\<game>`, macOS `~/Library/Application Support/<game>`, Android `.` (the app's own folder,
    which is the working directory). Point Steam Auto-Cloud at the same folder. Returns ""
    when `game` is empty, `.`, or holds `/`, `\` or `..`, or when the base variable is unset or the folder cannot be made.
    The string lives for the whole process (one page per call, so call it once). Any thread.
